# PitPat-T01 (SupeRun-built, service ffff) walking, 2026-11-18 local time (Europe/Rome).
# Not a daemon log: recorded in the browser with the PitPat Walk web app ("Record packets", Web
# Bluetooth), which keeps the raw bytes of every notification and write with a millisecond
# timestamp. Converted line by line to this format: the time is cut to the second, "notify" is a
# status notification, "write" a packet the page sent. The bytes are unchanged and include the
# 4d framing (4d 04 from the treadmill, 4d 00 from the host). Web Bluetooth does not expose the
# BLE address, so none is in the file; the 68 2f frame carries no serial.
# The belt was already running when the recording began and runs for the whole file. The page
# only wrote the framed keep-alive (4d 00 <seq> 05 6a 05 fd f8 43) every 200 ms: no start,
# SetSpeed, pause or stop in it.
# Three recordings back to back (the page saves one file per recording):
#   09:50:49-09:50:57 first recording (63 lines)
#   09:50:58-09:50:58 second recording (3 lines)
#   09:51:01-09:51:16 third recording (108 lines), ~3 s after the second
# Owner notes: 20 steps counted during the third recording, starting just after a step.
# Seen in the frames: the belt's step count (u16 @43) goes from 213 to 232 over the third
# recording; distance (@7) is metres despite the imperial flag (100 -> 110 m in those 15 s);
# speed and target (@3, @5) stay at 08 fc = 2300. Every notification is a 51-byte
# 4d 04 <seq> 2f frame around a 47-byte 68 2f packet; no other frame type appears (but the
# trace starts mid-walk, not at connect).
